{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Verified -1 on patchset 2 triaged: NOT a flake, and none of the known signatures. The failing\nstep was the module-size gate on all four pytest matrix jobs, reporting\n'814 src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py'.\n\nCause was my own error. 'git rebase --continue' created the commit containing the raw\n814-line conflict resolution, and every subsequent trim — moving the check into\n_tracker_health, sourcing pairs from EnvAuthorshipTally.identity_pairs(), deleting the two\nhelpers that became test-only — stayed in the WORKING TREE, uncommitted. I pushed the\nun-amended commit, so CI tested a tree I had never tested and my local 'wc -l' was measuring\ndifferent content than Gerrit had. A recheck would have failed identically every time.\n\nA second real failure surfaced on the rebased tree:\ntests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py::test_check_mode_clean_against_committed_tree. My commit\nand main each added one env var, so the textual merge kept both rows but resolved the count\nline to 160 instead of 161. Regenerated docs/env-vars.md (161, generator --check exit 0).\n\nBoth fixed and amended into patchset 3 (926bddb42d, rebased onto bb14781697). Process fix\nadopted: both CI gates are now verified against the COMMITTED tree via 'git archive HEAD'\nrather than the working tree — that is the check that would have caught the first miss.\nTargeted suite on the rebased tree: 9581 passed, the one registry failure now green."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786524926997202001,"uuid":"bb81add8-4ed0-4333-afdb-7f8421c79528"}